    "reviewMarkdown": "# UI Brief Review — employee-app-phase2\n\n## Scope\nExactly 8 pages from the signed PRD inventory: today, customer-search, customer-detail, appointment-detail, appointment-form, treatment-notice, appointment-list, callback-register. No additional pages or roles were introduced.\n\n## Gate fix\n- treatment-notice now declares `empty` in `requiredStates`, sets `emptyTitle` to 「暂无告知内容」, and keeps the confirm action hidden for empty content.\n- treatment-notice emits per-project `noticeBlocks` for 小气泡 and 补水 instead of flattening the notice text.\n- appointment-detail emits `businessStates` for 已登记、已到店、爽约、已取消 with every action a subset of `actions`.\n- appointment-form emits new/reschedule `formModes`; reschedule locks the customer.\n- appointment-list declares calendar/list `views` with calendar as `defaultView` and supplies four rows covering every field.\n\n## Data and labels\nEvery page field has a Chinese `fieldLabels` entry taken from the PRD field table. Detail pages have `mockData.values` for every field, list pages have 3–5 complete rows, and the home page has full `content` with store, quick actions, appointments, callbacks, and empty titles. Phone numbers are masked throughout.\n\n## Questions\nThere are zero blocking questions. Seven non-blocking review findings are recorded as questions and converted into matching assumptions A-001 through A-007. A-008 through A-011 capture mock-data, route, query-contract, and notice-copy assumptions.\n\n## Signoff\nThis candidate is ready for human brief signoff. The pipeline should record the canonical `briefHash` in `signoff/brief.md` before publishing the brief."
  },
